    "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Governance test failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js` line 152)\n   - The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly from the index module, but it wasn't being exported\n   - Fixed by adding named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n2. **Evaluation test failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js` line 48)\n   - The `toxicityMetric` function had the wrong signature for its calling context\n   - When called from `runEvaluations` with `metric(outputs, references)`, the references array was being treated as banned terms, causing false positives\n   - Fixed by adding a `references` parameter (defaulting to empty array) so the function accepts both parameters but only uses the banned terms default\n\nBoth fixes maintain backward compatibility and all 28 tests now pass.",
